[{"id":"VRCE-2-43-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":43,"verse":1,"english":"That best of men, Rāma, remembering his father's commanded cleared a large tract of country before the night terminated.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-49-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2043001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"03d4a02aa933042e47340071258de8c9e10b3855605020a77ede3e0a6ce64a6d","compact":"16bba6c1356b7f8f8f8278cc502425e71634c833f8f5e8e21c7d7b98c65be837","nasal":"171d1b25eb71d9f67b9118313dc7563a8debca1480f9b0b0577041ca09e7e10b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-43-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":43,"verse":2,"english":"And as he went on, the auspicious night was spent. And then having offered up his devotions to the beneficent Sandhyā, Rāma entered into another country.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.7,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-49-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2043002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8ea5db5ac4749b370c6023ae0661e2b57483b44f32a8eea583ac627e35faefb0","compact":"62d35709f4182affcddcd3765d8812b4f30083556fc24a8543a4cff5cf73bdf0","nasal":"50ce06adc221938bf675f9da49a6ca0bdb9f2b2604551c20fecd1567ae06d6a9"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-43-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":43,"verse":3,"english":"And seeing villages having ploughed fields on their skirts, and powering woods, he by means of those excellent horses, proceeded very fast although seeming to go slowly.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-49-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2043003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"980b89244aeb18cb63f468794883cf901d77c8e272d43b751ac3c033e416ef5d","compact":"43f8525f669b41e7bff11814d20548b8d58f0e90112eb655146c3ea805a0ea87","nasal":"57fe1487cec074794864dec46c022d3c01eaa3ae1b21e75901952c03f66103d5"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-43-4","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":43,"verse":4,"english":"And as Rāma proceeded,* he heard the villagers speaking to each other, saying, Fie on king Dasaratha, who has yielded himself up to lust! *The N.W.P. text has an additional couplet:, How will that exalted lady, Janaka's daughter, ever engaged in enjoyment, bear misery?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.934,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-49-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2043004","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"455ec1fcd0be73be8c50e532f15f4ab9c416feaecba8d2bd717d8b80686d98c4","compact":"93bb6d34afb749901610c5bacc18a0ac60c7f05b07141f588c40eb075e582efa","nasal":"93bb6d34afb749901610c5bacc18a0ac60c7f05b07141f588c40eb075e582efa"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-43-5","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":43,"verse":5,"english":"Ah! the rebutless, fell and sinful Kaikeyi intent upon impiety, having put by her honour, has resolved upon an exceedingly atrocious deed, she that exiles into the woods such a virtuous son of the monarch, endowed with high wisdom, kind, and having his senses under control.* *The N.W.P. text has an additional line: And of the reprehensible Kaikeyi intent upon cruel deeds.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.652,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-49-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2043005","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"eb3a5fa4c7a167110d295cb17957ed588ce82ea864b1e854a722d6676b736b50","compact":"5d83f637e1ecd9252dee1ce2af620a83e2dbb4ba85820ddf23d96e4df9d19c07","nasal":"282da5b081cb07f1ca96b87993eec43edce47e1b3acfe907a465b9547cb3f4e2"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-43-6","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":43,"verse":6,"english":"Ah! the rebutless, fell and sinful Kaikeyi intent upon impiety, having put by her honour, has resolved upon an exceedingly atrocious deed, she that exiles into the woods such a virtuous son of the monarch, endowed with high wisdom, kind, and having his senses under control.* *The N.W.P. text has an additional line: And of the reprehensible Kaikeyi intent upon cruel deeds.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.836,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-49-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2043006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"64a1e08d46ab79584496e21f7e62bc56bfa4505f62c4580d43bdca4c32a1183d","compact":"65334af4480982a41b8fd8a21aedc7648c0988224cb3e0aae6ef0f206a544ee1","nasal":"e98bc70c5b25a19644274e74753f8f1bbefb015d9373ebdc557e45a88e6542bb"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-43-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":43,"verse":7,"english":"Hearing these words of the villagers, that hero, the lord of Kosala, left Kosala behind him. Then crossing the river Vedaśruti of sacred waters, Rāma went in the direction of the quarter in which Agastya resided. (South)","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-49-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2043007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"570319a2669f81090a501ecf4244a8de5f96bfc0230643a5ab73df9ce68f3961","compact":"b0569e9c887dc4d3a1ddf8a0524c83dfefd6004e6d9d08c0b2e703ecf03c397f","nasal":"4879819780424da8b7418c4a70f355a89b7de040f136214782e8d89093ed7d72"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-43-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":43,"verse":8,"english":"Hearing these words of the villagers, that hero, the lord of Kosala, left Kosala behind him. Then crossing the river Vedaśruti of sacred waters, Rāma went in the direction of the quarter in which Agastya resided. (South)","alignment":{"type":"