e":11,"english":"Here Rāma showed to Vaidehi those flourishing regions that had formerly been conferred by king Manu on Ikşvāku, and which teemed with populous tracts.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.886,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-49-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2043011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"93c6c994b0b4e56618a916f1922c00dee8f87717c243448a0845bb61e33dbfb2","compact":"9b0989aaa666b27677cb2ac4a78f8e8821e915ad3668dc9f0aa5bb6b4c1046c5","nasal":"9b0989aaa666b27677cb2ac4a78f8e8821e915ad3668dc9f0aa5bb6b4c1046c5"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-43-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":43,"verse":12,"english":"Then frequently addressing the charioteer, saying, \"O Suta\", that best of men furnished with grace and endowed with a voice like that of a mad swan, spoke.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.915,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-49-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2043012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"663ca26fdf7c65edac416099d7dab6822505334c13056a7a94d5df659688b4ba","compact":"062448f62bdb1b64184bf35938faf0434908dc8f7d5cbc72bf8c56820dec04df","nasal":"062448f62bdb1b64184bf35938faf0434908dc8f7d5cbc72bf8c56820dec04df"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-43-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":43,"verse":13,"english":"When shall I coming back, range a hunting the blossoming groves of the Sarayū, along with my father and mother?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.852,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-49-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2043013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a2c23158f659e5bbed91bfac32c6034d9bda1f349782ea0c9a8c8de0da6f1e61","compact":"4560951586fe2514a1ef99b5b8d9e6fe57c33ff06e881b25f39962aa1c396064","nasal"